From 8d1c97cae48e39a7f9a4f3e07a11a8a9ab6c2b41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:13:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Lock screen, rules by window title, covers, hidden battery,
 real maximum

- While the screen is locked (the helper's .../locked) the bar shows a
  row of its own, Esc and LockScreenKeys (none by default): no
  notification, now-playing panel or slider of the session.
- MatchTitle in an [[Apps]] rule: parts of the window title (the helper's
  .../title), any of which must be in it; Match may be left out. A title
  change alone looks at the rules again, so a web site gets its own keys.
- The now-playing key and panel show the player's cover (nowplaying "art
  <file>", an SVG around the picture next to the state files); the
  scrubber starts after it.
- ShowBelow on a Battery key: shown only below that charge or while
  charging, taking no room otherwise.
- AdaptiveBrightness divides by the display backlight's own maximum, not
  Apple silicon's 509 (acpi_video0 here goes to 90: the bar was always on
  its lowest level).
- TINY_DFR_WHICH_SET takes "class|title" too.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M5fvpySRgDHQss3fsr2hF6

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
